d0cac4b1cbf87198e450c59c6084403bfe881369", "unit_id": "inventory:morphisms:07R4:lemma/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:cfe164b03e6d4ac6b078ed1f57942aba3ba91bc871a8583260e8d9001f44a8cd", "hash": "sha256:cfe164b03e6d4ac6b078ed1f57942aba3ba91bc871a8583260e8d9001f44a8cd", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 120326, "byte_start": 120181, "file": "morphisms.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:f9a972e2619735b0e8e85bc1f3987eb02090908bff68cf7702db0477581e854a", "line_end": 3307, "line_start": 3305}, "owner_tag": "07R2", "parent_tag": "07R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "07R2", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{more-algebra-definition-J}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9852dadd34b00d598b17f8a5ade3739bf4c63d3529b2a90cb3c7d03556d133f6", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is the analogue of the corresponding notion for Noetherian\nrings, see More on Algebra, Definition <REF_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:222cd96b47763282046aac7f16762426e7779b6c4d984a0f584f28b7962cef8c", "unit_id": "inventory:morphisms:07R2:paragraph/0002"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:de0d7a1bc372eeeae555b6413c965d2b0bd9c4bfa16322710bfe5f77216fcd21", "hash": "sha256:de0d7a1bc372eeeae555b6413c965d2b0bd9c4bfa16322710bfe5f77216fcd21", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 122189, "byte_start": 120848, "file": "morphisms.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:7635cc17ce19c13072b5339e23676c1d1027ba58e9cd5b2a543891b32ceaec03", "line_end": 3354, "line_start": 3325}, "owner_tag": "07R4", "parent_tag": "07R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "07R2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(R)$", "MATH_0004": "$R$", "MATH_0005": "$A$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0007": "$R$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0010": "$Y \\to X$", "MATH_0011": "$Y = \\bigcup V_j$", "MATH_0012": "$V_j \\to X$", "MATH_0013": "$U_i$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{O}(U_i) \\to \\mathcal{O}(V_j)$", "MATH_0015": "$V_j = \\Spec(\\mathcal{O}(V_j))$", "MATH_0016": "$\\text{Reg}(Y) \\cap V_j = \\text{Reg}(V_j)$", "MATH_0017": "$\\text{Reg}(Y)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-immersion-locally-finite-type}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-composition-finite-type}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{more-algebra-definition-J}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-locally-finite-type-characterize}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0005": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6dc87328a117435a296e56a0bdf53894c73a5bec1a318ddc29c3a1d2910415e0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:278c0afd303f3a327a972cb9c8ee822216170f94aa8ae60e6d904b9f8bf79ed6", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nBy Lemma <REF_0001> an open immersion\nis locally of finite type. A composition of morphisms locally of\nfinite type is locally of finite type\n(Lemma <REF_0002>). Thus it is clear that if <MATH_0001> is\nJ-2 then any open and any scheme locally of finite\ntype over <MATH_0002> is J-2 as well. This proves the final\nstatement of the lemma.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nIf <MATH_0003> is J-2, then for every finite type <MATH_0004>-algebra <MATH_0005>\nthe regular locus of the scheme <MATH_0006> is open. Hence <MATH_0007> is\nJ-2, by definition (see\nMore on Algebra, Definition <REF_0003>).\nCombined with the remarks above we conclude that (1) implies (3), and\n(2) implies (4). Of course (1) <MATH_0008> (2) and\n(3) <MATH_0009> (4) trivially.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nTo finish the proof we show that (4) implies (1).\nAssume (4) and let <MATH_0010> be a morphism locally of finite type.\nWe can find an affine open covering <MATH_0011> such that\neach <MATH_0012> maps into one of the <MATH_0013>. By\nLemma <REF_0004>\nthe induced ring map <MATH_0014> is\nof finite type. Hence the regular locus of\n<MATH_0015> is open. Since\n<MATH_0016> we conclude that\n<MATH_0017> is open as desired.\n<STRUCT_0006>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:69a49fc2831fbe38857703d19d312b522aaddec4932df7ad4722a47c77bc9bf3", "unit_id": "inventory:morphisms:07R4:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:d4a9876bd35f0ae8a785c3cae2286a2b2f9b2b51cb98de71dfdfc5b1b9d0304b", "hash": "sha256:d4a9876bd35f0ae8a785c3cae2286a2b2f9b2b51cb98de71dfdfc5b1b9d0304b", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 438485, "byte_start": 438088, "file": "more-algebra.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:5f37d9359ef2dbc91410fdd2961399026192d13dc8b9fb8a5620e8290f7bfb92", "line_end": 11593, "line_start": 11582}, "owner_tag": "07P7", "parent_tag": "07P6", "requested_label": "more-algebra-definition-J", "requested_tag": "07P7", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "more-algebra", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "07P6", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{definition-J}", "LOCKED_0002": "\\begin{reference}\n\\cite[(32.B)]{MatCA}\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$X = \\Spec(R)$", "MATH_0003": "$R$", "MATH_0004": "$\\text{Reg}(X)$", "MATH_0005": "$R$", "MATH_0006": "$\\text{Reg}(X)$", "MATH_0007": "$R$", "MATH_0008": "$R$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{definition}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{definition}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:83750455c458b5702bb8d3cd695020b0bfa78d4f6a92047ee9023922d885d1fc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ead56a82a98d967bfd1b0f71d1a8c20639c4a1e2c3c711b0d5387fe86081d429", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\n<LOCKED_0002>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a Noetherian ring. Let <MATH_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> We say <MATH_0003> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>J-0<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0004> contains a nonempty open.\n<STRUCT_0004> We say <MATH_0005> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>J-1<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if <MATH_0006> is open.\n<STRUCT_0005> We say <MATH_0007> is <TEXTITOPEN_0003>J-2<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> if any finite type <MATH_0008>-algebra is J-1.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n<STRUCT_0007>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:47577544f39ebecefe0cd2d30eec44dabb3af5c1da50e4a125d909ce2c305e6a", "unit_id": "inventory:more-algebra:07P7:definition/0001"}}}], "input_freeze": {"hash": "sha256:bde2d19767a6a803085bcfd26ae23f9ee4ad7bf11b5acfa0eb55cbec6a2d7fa9", "path": "translation-data/source-adoption-inputs/p1-29-morphisms-p015.json"}, "model_output": {"hash": "sha256:a86d84302f5732187c9220abd32525e07698b281ae742692310c9012e55c677f", "path": "docs/evidence/p1-29-morphisms-p015-raw-01.jsonl", "record_hash": "sha256:ceef710c88a4a786080ed19f7dc3d8dca629d41a1b3507948ce0e94a208003e1"}, "neighbor_unit_ids": ["tag:07R2:prose-0002"], "policy_revision": "git:c0c436b9d7ac86a6d277fd74ff439fd2389bdb84", "prior_generations": [], "prompt_version": "translator-v2", "source_adoption_id": "p1-29-morphisms-p015", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "style_guide_path": "config/style-guide.md", "turn_id": "01a21bb5-b1eb-7d22-882b-b6ebafab71e6", "unit_id": "tag:07R4:statement"}, "context_hash": "sha256:c023400451ba4ce62b00de236875a289ec9b1677aa42fe130560a37d48bec60d", "created_at": "2026-11-27T06:33:43.697Z", "glossary_revision": "git:c0c436b9d7ac86a6d277fd74ff439fd2389bdb84", "harness_id": "codex", "harness_version": "0.172.0", "model_id": "gpt-6.2-sol", "model_identity_confidence": "declared", "model_lane": "openai-gpt-6.2-sol", "model_record_id": "openai:gpt-6.2-sol:declared", "model_snapshot": null, "notes": [], "prompt_version": "translator-v2", "publication_status": "CANDIDATE", "qa_status": "PASS", "reasoning_effort": "high", "run_id": "run-p1-29-morphisms-p015", "schema_version": 2, "source_adoption_id": "p1-29-morphisms-p015", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_text_hash": "sha256:de05c95f1d41a9572b97c3bc813484114a646b7fe87695214a453754e13168f7", "stage": "STRUCTURE_OK", "term_occurrences": [{"source_term": "locally Noetherian", "target_term": "局部诺特"}, {"source_term": "scheme", "target_term": "概形"}, {"source_term": "equivalent", "target_term": "等价"}, {"source_term": "covering", "target_term": "覆盖"}, {"source_term": "schemes", "target_term": "概形"}, {"source_term": "affine open", "target_term": "仿射开集"}, {"source_term": "ring", "target_term": "环"}, {"source_term": "affine open", "target_term": "仿射开集"}, {"source_term": "covering", "target_term": "覆盖"}, {"source_term": "scheme", "target_term": "概形"}, {"source_term": "locally of finite type", "target_term": "局部有限型"}], "term_status": "DECISION_REQUIRED", "translation": "设<MATH_0001>是局部诺特（locally Noetherian）概形（scheme）。下列条件等价（equivalent）：\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002>是 J-2；\n<STRUCT_0003> 存在<MATH_0003>的一个开覆盖（covering），其每个成员都是 J-2 概形（schemes）；\n<STRUCT_0004> 对每个仿射开集（affine open）<MATH_0004>，环（ring）<MATH_0005>都是 J-2；\n<STRUCT_0005> 存在一个由仿射开集（affine open）组成的覆盖（covering）<MATH_0006>，使得每个<MATH_0007>都是 J-2，对所有<MATH_0008>均如此。\n<STRUCT_0006>\n此外，在这种情形下，<MATH_0009>上的任意概形（scheme）只要是局部有限型（locally of finite type）的，也都是 J-2。\n", "translation_hash": "sha256:66c579bac3550b75e86d0dfaf02eb4dd3cf0b3d9a5dbc5a041ca593393ef2f0d", "unit_id": "tag:07R4:statement", "unknown_terms": [{"context": "引理对给定概形的假设", "source_term": "locally Noetherian", "target_term": "局部诺特"}, {"context": "引理所考察的给定对象", "source_term": "scheme", "target_term": "概形"}, {"context": "说明所列条件相互蕴含", "source_term": "equivalent", "target_term": "等价"}, {"context": "第二项要求存在开覆盖", "source_term": "covering", "target_term": "覆盖"}, {"context": "第二项要求覆盖的每个成员都是 J-2 概形", "source_term": "schemes", "target_term": "概形"}, {"context": "第三项对每个此类开集作断言", "source_term": "affine open", "target_term": "仿射开集"}, {"context": "第三项中要求具有 J-2 性质的对象", "source_term": "ring", "target_term": "环"}, {"context": "第四项所要求的覆盖由此类开集组成", "source_term": "affine open", "target_term": "仿射开集"}, {"context": "第四项要求存在由仿射开集组成的覆盖", "source_term": "covering", "target_term": "覆盖"}, {"context": "附加结论所量化的对象", "source_term": "scheme", "target_term": "概形"}, {"context": "附加结论对概形在给定底概形上的有限性条件", "source_term": "locally of finite type", "target_term": "局部有限型"}]}
